    "created_at": "2022-12-03T04:01:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-12-03T04:04:31Z",
    "body": "I figured this was intentional because the concept of boolean presence vs absence content attributes is HTML-specific, not an XML thing, no?\r\n\r\n(I’d actually find this addition useful given the namespace-agnostic versions behave unsoundly when you don’t know whether other code is managing attrs with non-null namespaces, but am curious whether the omission may have been deliberate.)",
